00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:05.240
Oh... Morning.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.290
Good morning.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.790
His invincibility has ended.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:19.010
Although nothing had changed,
I felt I was temporarily set free.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:21.590
I bet it was my mind’s defense mechanism.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.140
Are you okay?

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.230
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:34.350
Hello!

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.780
I'm Iketeru Daga, your singer <i>oniisan</i>.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.700
I'm Utano Tadano, your singer <i>oneesan</i>.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.240
I'm Uramichi Omota, your gymnast <i>oniisan</i>.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:49.950
Let's have a <i>ton </i>of fun
singing and playing today!

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:54.330
First, we'll sing this song,
my favorite one!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:58.300
"How Come It Only Rains
When You Forget Your Umbrella?"

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:08.470
♬ The forecast said cloudy,
with a chance of rain. ♬

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:15.150
♬ My animal instincts
are being tested again. ♬

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.570
♬ How come it only rains ♬

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:25.070
♬ when you forget your umbrella? ♬

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:29.790
♬ When you don't,
it doesn't rain at all! ♬

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:33.960
♬ Even though there was
a pretty high chance of rainfall. ♬

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:42.920
♬ So this pointless umbrella
just weighs you down all day! ♬

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:47.760
♬ Always a tiny little bit in the way! ♬

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.350
♬ What a rain! ♬

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:50.680
"A tiny little bit in the way"
"What a rain"

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.510
"Move onto the next song!"

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:56.650
Next up is this song, which we
got many requests for last week.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:59.820
"Those Little Spiders
You See Around the House."

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.080
"Omota, Usao, Kumao"
"Put on a spider headgear, hold a huge cotton swab, and keep standing at the edge of the stage."

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:20.040
Do you... need me in this?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.920
I do! It's up to you,
as the spider, Uramichi-<i>kun</i>...

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.680
...whether this song can
capture the kids' hearts or not.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:31.850
Its success depends on the sorrow
of a spider who stares out into space...

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.270
...I think!

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:36.190
It'll make a difference
in the depth of the song...

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:37.350
...I think!

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:43.480
I don't get it... But...

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:48.200
...whatever your superior says, you need
to pretend that you understand it...

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.000
...because that's what adults do.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.970
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:12.100
Well then, next, we'll read
letters from friends!

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:12.170
Letter Time

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:12.170
Letter Time

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:17.230
The first letter is from Haruko-<i>chan</i>,
four years old, in Shimane Prefecture.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:22.440
"I have fun watching <i>Together with Maman</i>.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.360
When I grow up,

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:30.490
I want to marry someone like
Iketeru-<i>oniisan </i>or Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:36.910
Utano-<i>oneesan</i>. If you were to marry either
of them, which <i>oniisan </i>would you pick?

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.750
Well, I would say...

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.080
Hm?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.960
Haruko-<i>chan</i>! Don't choose a man
just for his good looks or humor!

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:50.720
Things like appearance or
friendliness might be charming.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:54.970
But despite that, they're not going
to be useful at all in the future!

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:59.020
Haruko-<i>chan</i>... Please avoid
unnecessary hardships!

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.270
Please be happy...

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.780
...with as few setbacks as possible.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:11.110
Okay! We'll stop here for now!

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:14.490
Since both <i>oniisans </i>had their feelings
hurt, we'll have them take a break!

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.950
m 540 174 l 825 174 827 329 540 326

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.950
Green Room
for Uramichi 
Omota-sama

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.290
I'm sorry.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:25.000
I kind of sounded like you two
were complete disasters.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.550
You didn’t “sound like” it,
you outright said it.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:31.510
More importantly, you both
have your own green room.

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:34.550
Please don't gather here.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.680
Aren't there times when you can't
bear the silence of being alone?

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.730
Yeah, every day.

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:44.020
But at least you live with someone.
That's better, isn't it?

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:49.860
Lately, when I buy <i>Ze**xy</i>
and bring it home,

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:53.780
he immediately puts his <i>Ju*p </i>on top of it.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.080
He’s telling you that
he doesn’t want to grow up.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.580
Shut up.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.620
"JUNP"
"ZETAXY"

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.540
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:06.340
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:11.010
It's time for <i>Together with Maman</i>!

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:14.800
Let's play together a lot today!

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.890
I think I'm going to work.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.820
Which animal do you like?

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:37.200
I like Tigers.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:39.910
Roar! Roar, roar!

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:43.330
I like horses!

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:48.090
Neigh! Brrrr... Neigh!

00:10:48.160 --> 00:11:00.680
"Gomilla"
"MHK Special Effect Drama"

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:51.710
Remind me, do you bet on horses?

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:55.430
No, I don't. I purely like them.

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:59.350
But you do like baseball,
right, Utano-<i>oneesan</i>?

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:00.560
Well, yeah.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:06.940
The year a cat barges onto the
baseball field will be a great one!

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:09.110
Please get ready for the show.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.780
As for me, I like...

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:14.990
...my "li'l buddy," the chinchilla.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:21.580
He's been harassing me
lately using this method.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:25.460
Yeah. You got in a lot of trouble
since you had so many bad takes.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:27.670
Oh, good morning!

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.710
Good morning.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.300
Good... morning.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:33.880
Hmm...

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.090
A "one-eyed snake"...

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.130
...or man's "best friend"...

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.970
...could've worked, too, huh?

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:41.640
You like them?

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.020
Not really.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.560
Dicks are everywhere...

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:53.070
Okay, this is the facilitator of the new
segment "Uramichi's Advice Room."

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:54.650
It's the little birdy.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:02.120
We designed it by using
your drawing as a reference.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.620
Tehehe.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.370
I won't give you permission to use it.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.670
Please change the design!

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:13.170
You need to take that up
with Director Derekida.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:19.260
Time for a new segment!

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:23.470
"Advice Room"

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:23.390
"Uramichi's Advice Room!"

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:25.680
Hello, little birdy!

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.690
I heard that you've got something
you want to ask me today?

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:32.060
I wonder what it is.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.690
Do you enjoy life?

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:38.820
Do you have any hobbies?
Besides weight training?

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:49.620
"He who runs after two hares
will catch neither"

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.170
F-Forgive me! I'm sorry!

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:02.510
I'm being forced to say those things!
Director Derekida told me to say them!

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:04.050
I didn't say that.

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.220
He said he wanted to skimp
on personnel expenses,

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:10.980
so, one of the costume roles had to do it.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.520
That, I did.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.730
Ah... um...

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:20.400
Dammit! That jerk Kumatani quickly
feigned being sick and ran off!

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.570
Palpitations, headache,
and abdominal pain,

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:27.490
nausea, dizziness, and hallucinations...
I had all those symptoms at once.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:34.710
Salmon

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:28.870
I'm doing okay now, though.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:32.040
When it comes to lying,
you sure are smooth!

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.000
Don't hide your face!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.590
Well, little birdy who likes to pick
on someone for not having hobbies...

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:42.090
Do you have any wonderful hobbies?

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:46.720
What? Is he continuing the segment?
As if nothing happened?!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:53.150
Name one other than reading,
watching movies, and listening to music.

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:54.440
What?!

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:58.650
Did you know that the people who
boast about having generic hobbies

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:02.910
end up getting exposed as having
no hobbies when asked for details?

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:05.910
At a group date, you start off saying to
someone, "Hey, we have the same hobby!"

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.990
You think you might hit it off with her.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.830
But just when she starts showing interest,

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:12.080
you gradually become unable
to keep up with her.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:14.040
Then, when you start panicking,

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:18.590
you realize that she's sitting far away
from you. Does that ring a bell?

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.090
Yes. A whole chorus of them.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:22.340
You also feel that you've completely lost

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:26.850
the curiosity and the drive
you need to master something

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:29.720
in the past ten years, right?

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:32.430
Yes, I do feel that.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:36.020
"When I grow up, I'll be able to do
whatever I want, whenever I want!"

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:41.070
You lived behind the wall representing
"freedom" with that hope as a child.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:44.150
You finally climbed over
that wall and became an adult,

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.950
but now, you are devoid of vitality.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:53.660
Kids! If you think no one else
but you may be constrained...

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:54.710
Don't worry!

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:59.040
You'll die if you swim in a tank
that’s too small, or too big!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.090
So, society must be
adjusting the tank well!

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:03.420
The end!

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.800
H-He wrapped it up...!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.550
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.720
Kids are coming in!

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:18.560
Hello!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.690
Before we start playing together,

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:25.700
there's something I'd like
to ask you kids. Is that okay?

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:26.570
Do you have to?

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.910
I guess I'll allow it.

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:30.950
Make it quick, okay?

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:34.080
What do you think of this?

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:39.420
Would you kids happen to prefer
cuter puppets or something?

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:42.250
What? You don't know when to give up.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:46.630
You must be trying to use
the kids to resolve your problem.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.510
What do you think?

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.480
Creepy.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:58.480
I know, right?!

00:15:58.480 --> 00:15:59.440
But...

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:00.980
Hm?

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:04.360
...he's your friend, right?

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:11.330
Mom told me to treasure my friends.

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:14.080
So, you should treasure your friend, okay?

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.950
Er... Okay.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.920
But... if possible...

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:23.050
...I think you should
make human friends, too.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.710
Yeah.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.260
Iketeru-<i>oniisan</i>.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.680
What? Oh, yes?

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:40.400
I guess you only notice the happiness
you feel from not hurting anywhere

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:44.320
when you're hurting somewhere, huh?

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.450
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>...

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.660
What in the world...

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.660
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.590
{=3}Sun

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.560
Sunday...

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:19.270
Right... no work today...

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:48.380
Hm?

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:13.820
Sorry.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:17.490
I guess I can't go home until
I catch your breakfast, huh?

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:29.960
Oh, I can't believe I let this happen.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:35.970
I'm out of olive oil when
I want to make <i>acqua pazza</i>.

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:38.430
I'll go to the supermarket,

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.640
so, wait here, okay, Sayuri-<i>san</i>?

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:50.190
There, there. Good girl, Sayuri-<i>san</i>.

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:52.280
I'll be right back, okay?

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.280
Be good, okay?

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:05.250
On second thought,
wanna come with me, Sayuri-<i>san</i>?

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:09.750
Supermarket Torima

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:17.340
"Amount per container: 400g
Best before (unopened):
Store at room temperature in dark place"

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:24.520
Frozen food is half-price,
so I'll buy some.

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:25.480
And that thing.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.520
"Olive Oil"

00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:28.190
Big Italian salami.

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:30.270
Hm? Huh? What the...?

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.740
Are you okay?

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:36.820
Y-Yes. It’s nothing.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:41.990
Oh, sorry. So, about
the salami... Salami is...

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.000
S-Sala--

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.460
Icy Slope Little Theater

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.460
Today's Tickets for Sale

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:53.630
So, when I noticed, I was asleep.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:55.470
What the heck?

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.540
Kadoma Amigos

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:01.970
Forget it!

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:02.810
Again...

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:05.060
...we are Kadoma Amigos!

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:07.390
Thank you very much!

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:16.400
What?! What'd you say?!

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:22.410
Hold on a sec! I can't hear you
at all, so I'll go outside!

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:24.200
"Wanna Quit Bunny"

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:24.120
What?!

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:29.630
Whoa! You caught some fish?
Then meet me up at Uramichi-<i>san</i>'s, okay?

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:27.250
"Pachinko Broke" "New machines are in"
"Takoyaki" "Croissant Taiyaki"

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:31.340
What? Pachinko?

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:33.920
Nah, I’m done.
I’ll just lose more if I stay.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.550
I bet Uramichi-<i>san </i>isn't
doing anything, anyway.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:41.430
He goes to the gym, drinks,
or makes curry. That's about all he does.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.310
What do you want?

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:46.980
Hello!

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:51.360
These are saké and <i>shochu </i>sent to me
by my parents, who run a liquor shop.

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:57.110
I also got some Croissant Taiyaki
at a stall in front of the pachinko place.

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:59.530
I don't like sweet stuff.

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:02.410
I like them, so...

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:04.280
Thanks for having me!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.460
Oh, Kumatani sounded
like he'd be here soon.

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:13.380
What'd you do today?

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:16.800
Nothing, really. I just went to the gym.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:18.220
I knew it.

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:19.840
Say what?

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.800
Ah... Well...

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:25.100
Oh, what time is it now?

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:28.640
The afternoon repeat might
be airing right now, right?

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:31.730
Now I'm going to read the last letter.

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:35.190
This is from Tooru-<i>kun</i>,
three years old, in Ehime Prefecture.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:36.610
Oh... That sucks. It's almost over.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:38.570
"I always watch <i>Together</i>
<i>with Maman </i>with my mom.

00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:38.570
Too bad.

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:45.450
When I grow up, I'd like to be
like the three of you and..."

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:41.860
Hm? All right! That's our Kumatani!

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:45.450
Perfect timing!

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:46.870
Ouch!

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:48.660
Ow, ow, ow...!

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:51.750
Ow, ow, ow... Dumbbells...!

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:54.960
Uramichi-<i>san</i>... You should
put your dumbbells away.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:58.130
I had a lot of fun today!

00:21:58.130 --> 00:22:03.260
Ow, ow... It hurts... It hurts like hell.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:04.800
What're you doing?

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:08.850
I hope you'll play a lot with us again!

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:11.770
Ouch!

00:22:11.770 --> 00:22:14.020
How many times do you have to hit them?

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:17.860
Okay, kids! See you next time!

00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:17.860
Ow... Ow...

00:22:17.860 --> 00:22:21.780
It hurts like hell!
My toes are broken for sure!

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:23.660
Uramichi-<i>san</i>!
